    },
    {
      "id": "f52d7f474-0",
      "kind": "gotcha",
      "text": "Due to how walkdir works if symlinks are not followed, symlinks to directories are seen as simple files by ripgrep.",
      "files": [
        "ignore/src/walk.rs",
        "tests/regression.rs"
      ],
      "commit": "52d7f474206eb517c7284448777ed839c0cae8bb",
      "split": "tune",
      "state": "live",
      "survival": 0.84
    },
    {
      "id": "f3d59bd98-0",
      "kind": "gotcha",
      "text": "The final \"dance\" is unnecessary, because by the time quitting begins, no thread will ever spawn a new `Work`.",
      "files": [
        "ignore/src/walk.rs"
      ],
      "commit": "3d59bd98aaea776092168f8feaf5daeeaf743cbf",
      "split": "tune",
      "state": "stale",
      "survival": 0.38
    },
    {
      "id": "f3d59bd98-1",
      "kind": "decision",
      "text": "The trick was to replace the heuristic spin-loop with blocking receive.",
      "files": [
        "ignore/src/walk.rs"
      ],
      "commit": "3d59bd98aaea776092168f8feaf5daeeaf743cbf",
      "split": "tune",
      "state": "stale",
      "survival": 0.38
    },
    {
      "id": "fee21897e-0",
      "kind": "decision",
      "text": "Once we have that, we just use 'qemu-foo rg' instead of 'rg'.",
      "files": [
        "tests/util.rs"
      ],
      "commit": "ee21897ebd35fc875a790b7ef0192609e81489f0",
      "split": "tune",
      "state": "live",
      "survival": 0.96
    },
    {
      "id": "ff314b0d5-0",
      "kind": "gotcha",
      "text": "It turns out that the previous version wasn't quite correct.",
      "files": [
        "crates/ignore/src/walk.rs"
      ],
      "commit": "f314b0d55f2fa7c9f19b677624a19a7ba24c7cf4",
      "split": "holdout",
      "state": "live",
      "survival": 0.96
    },
    {
      "id": "f0ea65efd-0",
      "kind": "gotcha",
      "text": "It turns out that using literals in this case when the -w flag is NOT used results in a performance regression.",
      "files": [
        "crates/regex/src/literal.rs"
      ],
      "commit": "0ea65efd6d7a98b721fcf5f62a6e549204ee01b2",
      "split": "holdout",
      "state": "unknown",
      "survival": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "f139f186e-0",
      "kind": "gotcha",
      "text": "While there are no real intrinsic differences, depth first traversal generally tends to use less memory because directory trees are more commonly wide than they are deep.",
      "files": [
        "crates/ignore/src/lib.rs",
        "crates/ignore/src/walk.rs"
      ],
      "commit": "139f186e5721e74542604fad8a3c5907c4911faa",
      "split": "tune",
      "state": "live",
      "survival": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "fa2e6aec7-0",
      "kind": "gotcha",
      "text": "Or more precisely, a new bug with the same root cause.",
      "files": [
        "tests/regression.rs"
      ],
      "commit": "a2e6aec7a4d9382941932245e8854f0ae5703a5e",
      "split": "holdout",
      "state": "live",
      "survival": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "f7ed9a318-0",
      "kind": "gotcha",
